- role: user
  content: |
    Now let’s discuss the requirements:
    - The system is deployed on the customer’s intranet and accessed via a web browser.
    - Login using initial owner username/password, with ability to modify credentials and add new admin or read-only user accounts.
    - Real-time display of readings from multiple monitoring devices in chart format.
    - Display historical trend curves for specified device readings with customizable time range; data exportable to CSV files.
    - Visual warnings displayed in yellow or red when readings exceed or fall below specified thresholds in the charts.
    - Clear visualization of the relationship between readings and warning thresholds in the charts.
    - Add/configure/delete monitoring devices, including reading units, sampling intervals, warning threshold rules, etc.
    - Group monitoring devices, with each group supporting the above charting interfaces.
    - Multi-language support (English and Chinese).
    - Clean and attractive interface with appropriate dynamic effects
    - Persistent data storage on the server.
    Can you clearly state the requirements from a user’s perspective and draft a document in specs/user?
